„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYBut he said unto them, All men cannot receive this saying, save they to whom it is given.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚFor there are some eunuchs, which were so born from their mother's womb: and there are some eunuchs, which were made eunuchs of men: and there be eunuchs, which have made themselves eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven's sake. He that is able to receive it, let him receive it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen were there brought unto him little children, that he should put his hands on them, and pray: and the disciples rebuked them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsBut Jesus said, Suffer little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom of heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3And he laid his hands on them, and departed thence.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd, behold, one came and said unto him, Good Master, what good thing shall I do, that I may have eternal life?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And he said unto him, Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God: but if thou wilt enter into life, keep the commandments.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—He saith unto him, Which? Jesus said, Thou shalt do no murder, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPHonour thy father and thy mother: and, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]The young man saith unto him, All these things have I kept from my youth up: what lack I yet?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸJesus said unto him, If thou wilt be perfect, go and sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come and follow me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_But when the young man heard that saying, he went away sorrowful: for he had great possessions.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThen said Jesus unto his disciples, Verily I say unto you, That a rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYWhen his disciples heard it, they were exceedingly amazed, saying, Who then can be saved?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmBut Jesus beheld them, and said unto them, With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuThen answered Peter and said unto him, Behold, we have forsaken all, and followed thee; what shall we have therefore?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙêAnd Jesus said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of man shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍAnd every one that hath forsaken houses, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my name's sake, shall receive an hundredfold, and shall inherit everlasting life.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCBut many that are first shall be last; and the last shall be first.¦layout ªlast_verse